Please write us letters, submit voice notes, maybe we'll read your letter on the air or or hear your voice at the start of an episode, but just tell us what, how I met your mother means to you or any other wonderful, how I met your mother related things you want to share with us.
请给我们写信，提交语音笔记，也许我们会在广播中读到您的信，或者在剧集开始时听到您的声音，但请告诉我们，我如何遇见你母亲对你意味着什么，或者任何其他与我如何遇见你母亲相关的精彩事情，你想与我们分享。

00:51:42.369 --> 00:51:45.220
Go to how we made your mother dot com contact.
请参阅我们如何与您的母亲 .com 取得联系。

00:51:45.220 --> 00:51:49.745
Is that right Alec and then everything should be pretty clear after that.
Alec 是这样吗？之后一切都应该很清楚了。

00:51:49.745 --> 00:51:50.245
Okay.
好的。

00:51:50.245 --> 00:51:53.530
So this is a wonderful letter we received from Emily.
这是我们从艾米丽那里收到的一封很棒的信。

00:51:53.900 --> 00:52:01.370
It says, December 2008, I was at the hospital delivery unit at the start of what was to be an almost 48 hour labor.
上面说，2008 年 12 月，我在医院分娩室开始了近 48 小时的分娩。

00:52:01.370 --> 00:52:10.139
My husband zipped out and returned with his laptop and season three of how I met your mother, which he'd quickly picked up at Best Buy.
我丈夫迅速出门，带着他的笔记本电脑和《我如何遇见你母亲》第三季回来了，他很快就在百思买买了这本书。

00:52:10.139 --> 00:52:16.699
We'd been watching together since in season one, I'd been a Buffy fan and follow it, Alison Hannigan.
我们从第一季开始就一起看，我是《巴菲》的粉丝并一直追随它，艾莉森·汉尼根。

00:52:16.699 --> 00:52:27.739
I'm sure we had already seen all of season three, but I remember us sitting on the hospital bed together waiting and waiting, and at least for a little while, pleasantly distracted with these great characters we do so well.
我确信我们已经看完了第三季的全部内容，但我记得我们一起坐在医院的病床上等啊等，至少有一段时间，我们愉快地被这些我们表现得如此出色的伟大角色所吸引。

00:52:27.739 --> 00:52:36.239
We'd also moved from New York a few years prior and reveled in the nostalgia for evenings with friends at our favorite bar, even while we looked toward our future.
几年前，我们也从纽约搬到了这里，纵然在展望未来的同时，我们仍沉浸在与朋友们在我们最喜欢的酒吧共度夜晚的怀旧之情中。

00:52:36.239 --> 00:52:43.549
I started re-watching this series this past January for the first time and came upon the new podcast on a subreddit.
去年一月，我第一次重新观看这个系列，并在 Reddit 子版块上发现了新的播客。

00:52:43.549 --> 00:52:44.809
Such perfect timing.
如此完美的时机。

00:52:44.809 --> 00:52:49.597
And imagine my delight as well to discover that I'd missed most of Season 8.
想象一下当我发现我错过了第八季的大部分内容时我有多高兴。

00:52:49.597 --> 00:52:51.803
My second child was an infant then.
那时我的第二个孩子还是个婴儿。

00:52:51.803 --> 00:52:55.898
It's also possible I did watch it, but just have no memory of it.
也有可能我确实看过，但只是不记得了。

00:52:55.898 --> 00:52:58.986
So it's like a whole lost season for me, rebound.
所以这对我来说就像是一个失去的赛季，反弹。

00:52:58.986 --> 00:53:00.435
Thank you for the show.
谢谢你的演出。

00:53:00.435 --> 00:53:04.027
It has a ton of heart and its creativity knows no bounds.
它有大量的心血和无限的创造力。

00:53:04.027 --> 00:53:12.659
I'm grateful to you all for putting this out in the world, even if I'm pretty sure it is behind my continued overuse of the word awesome.
我很感谢你们把这个公布于世，即使我很确定这是我继续过度使用“很棒”这个词的原因。

00:53:12.659 --> 00:53:13.478
You did good.
你做得很好。

00:53:13.478 --> 00:53:13.982
Be well.
祝你一切顺利。

00:53:13.982 --> 00:53:15.557
Emily from Oberlin, Ohio.
艾米丽来自俄亥俄州欧柏林。

00:53:15.557 --> 00:53:16.439
Thanks, Emily.
谢谢，艾米丽。

00:53:17.079 --> 00:53:18.057
Thank you, Emily.
谢谢你，艾米丽。

00:53:18.057 --> 00:53:19.034
That's fantastic.
太棒了。

00:53:19.034 --> 00:53:24.783
I love when people have like these core memories that have been formed around how I met your mother.
我喜欢人们拥有这些围绕我如何遇见你母亲而形成的核心记忆。

00:53:24.783 --> 00:53:29.612
Like we're our little show is part of the birth of her child and she remembers that.
就像我们的小节目是她孩子出生的一部分，她记得这一点。

00:53:29.612 --> 00:53:30.589
And that's great.
那太好了。

00:53:30.589 --> 00:53:40.305
In a very meta way, not to do spoilers, there is an episode of how I met your mother about distracting a pregnant woman who is in painful labor with storytelling, right?
为了不剧透，以一种非常元的方式，有一个关于我如何遇见你母亲的情节，是通过讲故事来分散一位正在痛苦分娩的孕妇的注意力，对吧？

00:53:40.305 --> 00:53:46.859
There's an episode just spoilers, we are constantly trying to figure out whether we're doing spoilers of the show.
有一集只是剧透，我们一直在努力弄清楚我们是否在剧透。

00:53:46.859 --> 00:53:55.655
But way later in the series, there is an episode where that's the idea of the episode, and now we're hearing how much mother fulfilled that role for her.
但在该系列的后期，有一集就是这一集的想法，现在我们听到母亲为她履行了多少角色。

00:53:55.655 --> 00:53:56.920
So that's really cool.
所以这真的很酷。

00:53:56.920 --> 00:54:04.490
I also think it's funny discovering like a lost treasure trove of how I met your mother episodes.
我还认为发现《我是如何遇见你母亲》的情节就像一个失落的宝库一样有趣。

00:54:04.490 --> 00:54:09.719
But I'm not sure I might have seen this, but I had no memory of it.
但我不确定我是否见过这个，但我不记得了。

00:54:09.719 --> 00:54:10.500
Think about it.
想一想。

00:54:10.500 --> 00:54:15.234
You didn't even know what your notes on this episode meant that you wrote last night, Josh.
你甚至不知道你昨晚写的关于这一集的笔记意味着什么，乔什。

00:54:15.234 --> 00:54:18.199
Now imagine it's basically a year of your life like that.
现在想象一下，这基本上就是你生命中的一年。

00:54:18.199 --> 00:54:26.349
But it's funny because one thing that I ascribed to how I met your mother super fans is an intense memory of every episode.
但这很有趣，因为我将与你妈妈的超级粉丝见面的方式归因于对每一集的强烈记忆。

00:54:26.349 --> 00:54:33.239
So it's really funny that the kind of mom brain would eradicate this It's the whole season in your head.
所以这真的很有趣，那种妈妈的大脑会根除你脑海中的整个季节。

00:54:33.239 --> 00:54:35.880
Yes, happens to dads too, to be fair.
是的，公平地说，这也发生在爸爸身上。

00:54:35.880 --> 00:54:36.880
Yeah.
是的。

00:54:36.880 --> 00:54:38.440
Thank you, Emily.
谢谢你，艾米丽。

00:54:38.440 --> 00:54:39.440
That's awesome.
太棒了。

00:54:39.440 --> 00:54:41.719
We're so honored to have been a part of your labor.
我们很荣幸能成为你们工作的一部分。

00:54:41.719 --> 00:54:44.000
It's a weird sentence, but we are.
这是一个奇怪的句子，但我们确实如此。

00:54:44.000 --> 00:54:46.400
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:54:46.400 --> 00:54:48.320
Please equip me.
请装备我。

00:54:48.320 --> 00:54:52.920
All sins are forgiven in New York City.
在纽约市，所有的罪孽都被宽恕。

00:54:52.920 --> 00:54:58.480
